// The smallest Yooperlang program.
//
// Every executable starts at `main`, which returns an int32 exit code
// (0 means success, like in C). `printf` is always in scope - it lowers
// to C's printf under the hood.
//
// Compile and run:
//   node ./src/yoopiler.js examples/intro/hello.yoop
//   ./examples/intro/hello

function main(): int32 {
    printf("Hello from Yooperlang!\n");
    return 0;
}

// expected output:
// Hello from Yooperlang!
